// HistoryHost412–782 retains HANDLE ownership, zeroed target-width OVERLAPPED,
// one-byte exclusive immediate locks, raw UTF16/reparse checks, held directory
// identity and child confinement, full rename header+tail, delete disposition,
// FlushFileBuffers and first-error semantics. Runtime owns all C layouts.
// The owner-approved NT relative-child and handle-identity cutover remains the
// canonical backend, not a duplicate of the old pathname child-open policy.

